# OpenJ5 Mosquitto ACL
# Pattern-based access control for robot topics.
#
# IMPORTANT: rules placed before any `user <name>` line are GLOBAL and apply
# to every client, including anonymous ones. Mosquitto does NOT match the
# `user anonymous` section against username-less clients (verified on real
# deployment 2026-08-26): anonymous grants must be declared here at top level.

# --- GLOBAL RULES (all clients, incl. anonymous on the localhost listener) ---
topic read $SYS/broker/version

# Healthcheck roundtrip topic (localhost listener only; harmless by design)
topic readwrite openj5/healthcheck/#

# --- PER-USER RULES ---

# Robot Core (node1) has full access
user node1
topic readwrite openj5/#
topic readwrite $SYS/#

# Head node (node2) - control and status (topics from config/common/topics.json)
user node2
topic readwrite openj5/v1/head/#
topic read openj5/v1/system/#

# Right arm node (node3)
user node3
topic readwrite openj5/v1/right_arm/#
topic read openj5/v1/system/#

# Left arm node (node4)
user node4
topic readwrite openj5/v1/left_arm/#
topic read openj5/v1/system/#

# Torso node (node5)
user node5
topic readwrite openj5/v1/torso/#
topic read openj5/v1/system/#

# Tracks node (node6)
user node6
topic readwrite openj5/v1/tracks/#
topic read openj5/v1/system/#

# Balance node (node7, ADR-017) - logical commands, state, telemetry, E-stop
user node7
topic readwrite openj5/v1/balance/#
topic read openj5/v1/system/#

# ROS2 bridge
user rosbridge
topic readwrite openj5/#

# Monitoring
user monitoring
topic read openj5/#
topic read $SYS/#

# API user
user api
topic readwrite openj5/#
